+## Receipts
+
+Four removal receipts, and no others: `pushed`, `moved-to-obsidian`,
+`stale`, `metadata-prune`. No receipt, or any doubt, is `NOT-SAFE`.
+A tool line is a receipt only when it satisfies the rule below. A
+looser tool line does not waive this section or Refuses.
+
+- `pushed`: the path exists, and its introducing commit
+  (`git log --diff-filter=A --format=%H -1 -- <path>`) is an ancestor of
+  the default remote-tracking ref. Resolve that ref from existing refs
+  only: `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` when it resolves, else the single
+  `refs/remotes/origin/*` branch ref if exactly one exists. No
+  remote-tracking ref → `NOT-SAFE(pushed-unverifiable)`. Local
+  `refs/heads/*`, including `master`, never establishes `pushed`. Do
+  not assume `origin/main`. No `git fetch`. Dirty or missing at act
+  time → not a receipt (see Refuses).
+- `moved-to-obsidian`: a ledger row whose source path and vault path
+  are absolute, both sha256 fields are lowercase hex-64, both re-hash
+  to the current bytes (vault side read-only), the two paths are not
+  the same file, and the vault copy is not inside the source tree. Any
+  symlink in either digest scope → `NOT-SAFE(symlink-present)`. The
+  Obsidian CLI is not a receipt. A row alone is not a receipt.
+  Secret-shaped components on either path → not a receipt, even if a
+  tool hashed them. `tools/souji-vault-verify.sh` is the receipt of
+  record for this class; a `moved-to-obsidian` line from
+  `tools/souji-verify.sh` alone is not sufficient (it does not enforce
+  absolute paths, lowercase hex-64, source-equals-vault, or
+  vault-inside-source).
+- `stale`: scratch-shaped — a `.scratch` path component, or basename
+  `*.out`, `*.log`, `*-draft.*`, `*checkpoint*.json`,
+  `*checkpoint*.png`, `*ckpt*.json`, `*ckpt*.png`, `*.ckpt`, or
+  `launch-*.json` — AND a reference sweep of the owning repo returns
+  zero hits AND mtime older than the decision threshold (tool default
+  `--stale-days 1`). The sweep counts hidden files. It excludes `.git`,
+  `souji-shokunin/census/**`, `souji-shokunin/tests/**`, and
+  `.ufo-quarantine/**`, and it does not open secret-shaped paths; an
+  unreadable or secret-shaped hit is `NOT-SAFE`, not zero refs. A
+  `stale` line from a tool whose sweep omits hidden files is not a
+  removal receipt.
+- `metadata-prune`: the path is a non-main `worktree <path>`
+  registration, the directory is absent, unique commits
+  (`git log --oneline <HEAD> --not --all`) are 0, and it is not a named
+  branch with commits absent from `refs/remotes/*`
+  (`git log --oneline <branch> --not --remotes`). That named-branch
+  case is `NOT-SAFE(unpushed-branch)` and stays locked until the branch
+  is pushed or the operator dispositions it. A present directory is
+  never `metadata-prune` (dirty → `NOT-SAFE(dirty)`; clean →
+  `NOT-SAFE`).
+- A directory containing `.git` (a repo root) is not `pushed`, `stale`,
+  or `metadata-prune`. The only receipt that can cover it is
+  `moved-to-obsidian`.
 
